# Normalize every text file to LF on checkin. This project is developed
# on Windows (Git for Windows), but .sh scripts run inside Linux
# containers -- a CRLF shebang line ("#!/bin/bash\r") fails to exec at
# all. text=auto lets git decide text vs. binary per file; eol=lf forces
# LF for whatever it decides is text, including .cmd (cmd.exe on any
# modern Windows tolerates bare LF fine, and one universal rule is
# simpler than carving out a CRLF exception for no real benefit).
* text=auto eol=lf
